\[b(T=0) =-\frac{3\lambda^{2}}{32}\sum_{l,m=1}^{2}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\int\biggl{\{} \frac{|\mathbf{k}|^{2}+m_{a}}{(|\mathbf{k}|^{2}+m_{a})^{2}+\gamma^{2}[\xi_{l,n}^ {(m)}(\mathbf{k})]^{2}}\] \[\times\mathrm{sgn}[\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})]+\frac{2}{\pi} \frac{\gamma\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})}{(|\mathbf{k}|^{2}+m_{a})^{2}+\gamma^{ 2}[\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})]^{2}}\] \[\times\ln\biggl{[}\frac{\gamma|\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})|}{| \mathbf{k}|^{2}+m_{a}}\biggr{]}\biggr{\}}\Delta_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})\frac{ d\mathbf{k}}{(2\pi)^{2}}, \tag{101}\]

where we have used the identity \(\theta(-x)=\frac{1}{2}[1-\mathrm{sgn}(x)]\) in order to simplify the above equation.

### \(\Theta_{II}\)-loop-current (LC) order parameter

The mean-field equation for the loop-current order parameter can be simplified following the same procedure outlined above. First of all, we transform the Matsubara sum in Eq. (33) into a integral over the complex plane. This leads to

\[R_{II}(T) =\frac{V_{pd}}{2}\sum_{l,m=1}^{2}\int\biggl{\{}-\frac{1}{2\pi i} \oint_{\mathcal{C}_{1}}dzn_{F}(z)\biggl{[}\frac{1}{h_{l}^{(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})}\] \[\times\frac{\partial h_{l}^{(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})}{\partial R_{II}}+ \frac{1}{\overline{h}_{l}^{(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})}\frac{\partial\overline{h}_{l}^ {(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})}{\partial R_{II}}\biggr{]}\biggr{\}}\frac{d\mathbf{k}}{(2 \pi)^{2}}. \tag{102}\]

Then we expand the terms between brackets in the above equation in a series of partial fractions, i.e.,

\[\frac{1}{h_{l}^{(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})}\frac{\partial h_{l}^{(m)}(z, \mathbf{k})}{\partial R_{II}}+\frac{1}{\overline{h}_{l}^{(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})} \frac{\partial\overline{h}_{l}^{(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})}{\partial R_{II}}\] \[=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\frac{\Xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})}{z-\xi_{l,n}^{(m )}(\mathbf{k})}, \tag{103}\]

where the coefficients of the expansion \(\Xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})\) are given by

\[\Xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k}) =\frac{\frac{\partial h_{l}^{(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})}{\partial R_{II}} \biggl{|}_{z=\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})}}{\frac{\partial h _{l}^{(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})}{\partial z}\biggl{|}_{z=\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})}}, \quad 1\leqslant n\leqslant\frac{N}{2}; \tag{104}\] \[\Xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k}) =\frac{\frac{\partial\overline{h}_{l}^{(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})}{ \partial R_{II}}\biggl{|}_{z=\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})}}{\frac{\partial \overline{h}_{l}^{(m)}(z,\mathbf{k})}{\partial z}\biggl{|}_{z=\xi_{l,n}^{(m)} (\mathbf{k})}}, \quad\frac{N}{2}+1\leqslant n\leqslant N. \tag{105}\]

Having in mind the result in Eq. (103), we evaluate the complex integral in Eq. (102) as

\[-\frac{1}{2\pi i}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})\oint _{\mathcal{C}_{1}}dz\frac{n_{F}(z)}{z-\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})}\] \[=\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})n_{F}[\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}( \mathbf{k})]. \tag{106}\]

Lastly the mean-field equation for the loop-current order parameter at finite temperature is obtained by inserting Eq. (106) into Eq. (102). Therefore this yields

\[R_{II}(T)=\frac{V_{pd}}{2}\sum_{l,m=1}^{2}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\int\Xi_{l,n}^{(m)}( \mathbf{k})n_{F}[\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})]\frac{d\mathbf{k}}{(2\pi)^{2}}. \tag{107}\]

In the limit of zero temperature, this equation becomes

\[R_{II}(T=0)=\frac{V_{pd}}{2}\sum_{l,m=1}^{2}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\int\Xi_{l,n}^{(m)}( \mathbf{k})\theta[-\xi_{l,n}^{(m)}(\mathbf{k})]\frac{d\mathbf{k}}{(2\pi)^{2}}, \tag{108}\]

with \(\theta(-x)\) being the Fermi-Dirac distribution function \(n_{F}(x)\) in this case.

